# Base URL for the API.
#
# Intentionally empty — this is correct for development: axios uses baseURL ""
# and requests relative paths (/api/...). The browser sends them to the same
# origin that serves the page, where the Vite proxy (vite.config.js) forwards
# them to the API after stripping the /api prefix.
#
# Leaving it empty is better than pointing to http://localhost:5293:
# same origin means no CORS, no preflight, readable Content-Disposition,
# and cookies that work without SameSite=None.
#
# In production:
#   - SPA behind the same reverse proxy as the API  -> leave empty
#   - API on a different domain                       -> VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
VITE_API_URL=